    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not just about the 50/60 hz base. i'm talking about the micro-fluctuations, the subtle harmonics they layer on top of the main carrier wave. if you look at the way they've standardized everything to 440hz in audio, it's clearly part of a larger pattern of using resonance to disrupt higher cognitive functions. if the grid was truly optimized for efficiency, they wouldn't need these specific, jittery deviations that cause so much unexplained fatigue in the population. don't you think it's suspicious how much the \"official\" physics textbooks ignore the psychological impact of these specific modulation patterns?",
